  "structural_change": "Q-DIE11-RLY 10-18 (coordinator HANDOFF 0ea item 1, LANDING-CONTRACT): 600-b forwarded-clock lane frame qfd_landh0_600_NE_104x106: landing with the hop-0 gate (rtl/qwen_split/qfd_fwd_lane.sv); replaces the regional-root qfd_rly_600 relay of the same die frame and faces. Recipe 4 flop-first, hold_budget die, M5 cap. QK-FWD 10-18 CLASS MASTER (tools/qwen_split/fwd_lane_classes.py): one hardened master per family / width class (1, 128, 600; widths quantised up, spare inputs tied low by the die) / direction class (H, V, HV, VH; the die places the rep with MX / MY / R180) / frame; replaces the per-GEN-frame masters (147 on dv2f14bn, 164 on dv2f14bg -> 48 classes). | QK-LANDEN 10-19 e1 (coordinator Q.STA.LAND600.3 option (b), ROOT-RST rule): en (hop-0 ICG enable = the source released reset) is registered on ck_s at the face (one async-clear flop) before the clock gate; the ICG enable and the ring write epoch are that flop, never the input port. +1 reset-release edge (K + 1 in the die calendar, lane_groups.HOP0_EN_REG); steady-state lane latency unchanged. Lane input min credits the lane_ckf tree (f20c82b74); io_hold_margin 0.03.",
